ssbook><name>NAKAGAWA, TOKIHARU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YUTANI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGASHIDA TAKAAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>INOUE KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KADORIKU SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI YOSHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MARUYAMA YOSHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA TOKIHARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YUTANI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGASHIDA, TAKAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOUE, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KADORIKU, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI, YOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MARUYAMA, YOSHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAGAWA, TOKIHARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YUTANI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical disk molding device and method that do not damage data formed in a molding and prevent decline in the quality of the molding. The device comprises a metal mold mover (136), a first gas feeder (134) and a controller (161), and it is arranged that the mold clamping is followed by the mold opening involving a travel distance (172) that will not damage the data-transferred surface (173) of the optical disk, thus forming a first separating space (175) and at the time when the first separating space has been formed, gas is fed to the first separating space to separate the optical disk and a stamper (115) from each other over the entire surfaces. Therefore, at the time when the first separating space has been formed, no damage has been caused to the data-transferred surface. After formation of the first separating space, since separation of the optical disk and stamper is effected by gas pressure, there is no damage caused to data throughout the data-transferred surface of the optical disk.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne un dispositif et un procédé de moulage pour disques optiques qui évite d'endommager les données formées pendant le moulage, sans perte de qualité au niveau du moulage. Le dispositif comprend un chargeur de moules métallique (136), un premier dispositif d'alimentation en gaz (134) et un organe de commande (161). IL est disposé manière à ce que la prise du moule et son ouverture subséquente se font sur une distance de déplacement (172) telle que la surface du disque optique (173) sur laquelle des données ont été transférées n'est pas endommagée. Au moment où cette surface est formée, on envoie du gaz dans un premier espace de séparation (175) pour séparer le disque optique du graveur (115) sur la totalité des surfaces. Ainsi, lorsque le premier espace de séparation est formé, la surface de transfert des données reste indemne. Après formation de ce premier espace de séparation, et comme la séparation du disque optique et du graveur se fait par pression gazeuse, aucun dégât n'est infligé aux données sur l'ensemble de la surface de transfert de données du disque optique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>